WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:12.668
The four classic synthesizer shapes are the sine, the square, the triangle and the sawtooth. They all have the same pitch; their timbre changes.

2
00:00:13.069 --> 00:00:22.937
The sawtooth has every harmonic, with an amplitude that falls as one over n: the second is half, the third a third. It sounds bright, like bowed strings.

3
00:00:25.486 --> 00:00:31.737
The square has only odd harmonics, which also fall as one over n. It sounds hollow, similar to a clarinet.

4
00:00:34.286 --> 00:00:43.405
The triangle also has only odd harmonics, but they fall as one over n squared: the third is one ninth. That is why it sounds soft, almost like a sine.

5
00:00:45.954 --> 00:00:54.609
In short: the sine is a single harmonic; the sawtooth has them all; the square and the triangle, only the odd ones, with different slopes.
